WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:05.040
The Alien movies are some of the scariest
and best-looking sci-fi horror movies ever

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.040
made.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:10.040
Unfortunately, while the Xenomorph queen might
be unkillable, it doesn't look like the franchise

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:11.440
has quite the same luck.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.300
Here's why we're afraid that Alien 5 might
never make it to the big screen.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:20.840
When Ridley Scott revealed that he was developing
prequels to Alien it was a huge day for fans

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.250
of the franchise, but maybe we shouldn't have
gotten so excited.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:29.220
2012's Prometheus wasn't exactly a disaster,
but the numbers it posted at the domestic

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.310
box office were a cause for concern.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:36.680
"A king has his reign, and then he dies.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.600
It's inevitable."

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:45.590
The movie failed to recoup its $130 million
budget domestically, though success in overseas

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:48.180
markets just about made a sequel viable.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:53.570
2017's Alien: Covenant wound up underperforming
both critically and commercially, however,

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:56.150
leaving the status of the franchise in jeopardy.

00:00:56.150 --> 00:01:00.760
Scott was open about his plans to start filming
a sequel within a year of Covenant's release,

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.775
but it doesn't seem like the box office returns
were good enough for him to get a green light

00:01:03.775 --> 00:01:04.775
from the studio.

00:01:04.775 --> 00:01:10.570
Of course, no more Alien prequels doesn't
necessarily mean no more Alien sequels, but

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:14.940
confidence and interest in the series is low
following Covenant, echoing the fallout that

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.610
followed 1997's disastrous Alien: Resurrection.

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:22.390
The franchise was put back into back hypersleep
for years, and the same could be happening

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:23.380
right now.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:28.860
H.R. Giger's contribution to the Alien franchise
has been well-noted, but Scott is of the belief

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:33.180
that Giger's iconic creation has now lost
its ability to scare audiences.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.970
He told Hollywood Reporter that:

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:37.600
"I think the beast has almost run out, personally...

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.560
You've got to come in with something else.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:43.820
You've got to replace that."

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:48.170
The franchise is named and based around the
existence of this vicious alien, so if it

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:52.430
just isn't scary anymore, is there even any
point in making an Alien 5?

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:56.640
It was terrifying in its day, but maybe it's
possible that it takes more than a creature

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.720
from outer space to excite audiences.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.280
Meanwhile, one of the biggest complaints Alien
fans had with Prometheus?

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.060
The lack of Xenomorphs.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:17.080
Scott attempted to remedy that with Covenant,
bringing the Alien back for another go despite

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:20.530
the director's earlier claims that the creature
wasn't scary anymore.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:24.190
It was a fickle move that didn't go unnoticed
by fans or critics.

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:27.920
After the film flopped, he reverted to his
original stance and stressed that he wanted

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.250
the franchise to explore artificial intelligence.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.120
"I don't understand."

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:38.360
"I guess that's because I'm a human being,
and you're a robot."

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:42.700
And even though he did bring the Xenomorphs
back in Covenant, much of the focus remained

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:45.260
on Michael Fassbender's android, David.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:50.210
Scott even clarified that any further prequels
would keep the focus squarely on the androids.

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:54.640
Scott laid out a vision for a planet led by
David, but that vision sounds closer to Blade

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.260
Runner than it does Alien.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:00.200
The further the franchise drifts away from
its roots, the less likely it is we'll ever

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.940
see round 5 of Ripley versus the Xenomorph.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:08.020
While Alien films could still be released
under the Fox studio name in the coming years,

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:12.710
they'll probably be made under the supervision
of its soon-to-be parent company Disney.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:16.730
Alien is one of the many properties that Disney
will have access to when it fully completes

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:21.850
its takeover of Fox, which is a cause of concern
for some, Ridley Scott included.

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:26.660
Speaking to Digital Spy, the veteran filmmaker
expressed concern over what rating any future

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:28.300
Alien movies would shoot for.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.650
"I've been with Fox for a number of years
now.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:34.600
I'm hoping I'll still probably be there, so
whether or not [Disney] go ahead with such

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.890
a dark subject as Aliens remains to be seen."

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:42.030
Disney's got a lot of franchises it's juggling
at the moment: The Marvel Cinematic Universe

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:47.000
continues to dominate Hollywood, and Star
Wars isn't exactly a small franchise either.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:51.120
That's not even mentioning any of their many
other films and projects, all of which might

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:54.569
get in the way of pushing out more Alien films
any time soon.

00:03:54.569 --> 00:03:59.030
Disney has a lot going on and will no doubt
be wary of messing with Alien canon, whether

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:01.840
that be with Scott's prequels or any potential
sequels.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:06.380
Ridley Scott isn't the only director who could
have made Alien 5.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:10.430
Neill Blomkam, the director of District 9,
was in talks to direct a sequel that would

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:15.430
have picked up immediately after Aliens, avoiding
the baggage from Alien 3 and Resurrection.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:19.650
Both Sigourney Weaver and Michael Biehn would
have returned as Ripley and Hicks, and Biehn

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:24.230
even floated the possibility of Newt coming
back as a 27-year-old woman.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.860
"Can I dream?"

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:28.620
"Yes, honey.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:33.000
I think we both can."

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.930
Fans hoped that this long-awaited sequel would
inject some new acid blood into the fading

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:37.930
franchise.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:38.930
So what happened?

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:41.210
In two words: Alien Covenant.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:45.190
Blomkamp said that preparation for his sequel
really got going in 2015.

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:48.800
This was around the time that Ridley Scott
had just finished his work on critical and

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:53.750
commercial sci-fi smash The Martian, leaving
him with an open slate waiting to be filled.

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:57.710
This effectively gave the studio a choice,
and they sided with Scott's prequels over

00:04:57.710 --> 00:04:59.110
a Blomkamp sequel.

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:05.740
In January 2018, Blomkamp tweeted out that
the Alien 5 project was 100% dead and buried,

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:07.340
and that he had moved on to other work.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.520
There's a really good reason that Neill Blomkamp
wanted his movie to take place after James

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:16.600
Cameron's Aliens, the first sequel to Ridley
Scott's original.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:21.240
1992's Alien 3 was trashed by the majority
of critics, who praised director David Fincher

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:25.680
for taking some admirable risks but concluded
that too few of them paid off in this plot

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:27.020
hole-riddled script.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:28.650
Why did the ship crash land?

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:32.570
If the ship's sensors picked up the fire,
then why didn't the ship's sprinkler system

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:33.570
activate?

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:36.300
How did the egg even get on the ship after
the events of Aliens?

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:41.270
Alien 3 left us with more questions than answers
and the very premise of the movie was dubious.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:45.860
Alien: Resurrection was only slighter better
received, with a story that made little sense

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:48.889
and a bizarre escalation of the classic Alien
design.

00:05:48.889 --> 00:05:53.389
In fact, the most impressive and memorable
moment in Resurrection belongs entirely to

00:05:53.389 --> 00:05:57.680
Sigourney Weaver sinking a basketball through
the basket behind her back, without the help

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:58.920
of special effects.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:12.380
Ridley Scott ignored all Alien films not directed
by him when he began work on his prequels,

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:15.449
and 2017's Covenant more or less erases them.

00:06:15.449 --> 00:06:19.220
At this point, nobody really knows where Alien
5 would fit into all of this.

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:23.620
When he revealed that Hicks and Newt were
potentially returning in Neill Blomkamp's

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:28.620
planned Alien 5, Michael Biehn also suggested
that Sigourney Weaver would be bowing out

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:32.650
in favor of a new lead who would be able to
carry the franchise going forward.

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:36.190
Speaking to Icons of Fright in 2015, Biehn
said that:

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:39.760
"They’re planning on bringing me and Newt
back, and at this point, Newt will be around

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:40.890
twenty-seven years old.

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:44.699
I know that every actress in Hollywood is
going to want to play this one, it’s really

00:06:44.699 --> 00:06:48.910
a passing of the torch between Sigourney and
this younger actress who would play Newt.

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:52.760
It would keep the franchise alive, and the
studios would make money, because that's what

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.360
the bottom line is now: money."

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:56.910
"I ain't here to be your friend.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:59.930
I'm here to make money.

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:01.750
You got that?"

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:06.199
It doesn't look as though Newt will be returning
any time soon, but Biehn is right about one

00:07:06.199 --> 00:07:10.070
thing: money talks in Hollywood, and franchise
longevity is key.

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:14.070
Would bringing Sigourney Weaver back for another
run out as Ripley achieve that?

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:18.400
It would probably be easier for Disney to
simply wipe the slate clean and start over

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:22.990
with the Alien franchise, putting the prequels,
original series, and any chance of an Alien

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:24.020
5 to bed.

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:28.440
In fact, prior to the acquisition deal with
Disney, Fox was reportedly planning on doing

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:29.440
just that.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.020
But who said the reboot had to be on the big
screen?

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:38.210
Fresh rumors of a TV show set in the Alien
universe emerged in April 2018.

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:42.960
It was welcome news for fans after Blomkamp's
Alien 5 died, but things went quiet in the

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:47.270
months that followed, making the rumors seem
less like insider information and more like

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:48.560
eager fan predictions.

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:53.080
Fox was never likely to greenlight an Alien
television show with the Disney deal looming

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:54.080
large.

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:57.820
However, now that the merger it basically
a done deal, Disney might just go ahead and

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:58.820
do it for them.

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:02.650
We know that Disney is heavily investing in
an upcoming streaming service in an effort

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:05.600
to establish a foothold in the Netflix-dominated
field.

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:10.830
The new service will boast original Marvel
and Star Wars shows when it goes live in 2019,

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:13.970
and adding an Alien series to the mix could
only add to the hype.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:18.740
It might not be Alien 5 but you may be seeing
more of your favorite acid-blooded, deadly

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:21.760
Xenomorph queen sometime soon on the small
screen.

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:25.720
"Get away from her, you BITCH!"

